posts.body:
Hey, folks. I've searched high and low and gotten close, but no cigar. I simply want to hide the actor's names on the battle screen and leave the portrait and other elements. ChatGPT says to pop this into a plugin, and I did that, but the name still appears in the Battle Status window.
Window_BattleStatus.prototype.drawActorName = function(actor, x, y, width) {
// this.drawText(actor.name(), x, y, width, 'left'); // Comment this line to hide the name
};
Looks like it makes sense, I think? I even tried blindly tweaking parts of it, but the name is still there.
...or should I just download a big, fat, battle customization plugin with all the bells and whistles in case I want to change something else, too? (I feel guilty posting in here.) That seems a bit overkill, though, when I don't have many big problems with MZ's battle interface otherwise. At least, any I haven't already fixed with a handful of tiny plugins.
Thanks so much!
